│   ├── unit_check
│   └── consistency_check
│
└── formatter/
    ├── twelve_hour
    └── twenty_four_hour
```

## 57. Complete Reasoning Example

Input:

> “A train leaves at 11:40 PM. It travels for 2 hours and 35 minutes. When does it arrive?”

### Step 1 — Detect time

```text
11:40 PM
```

### Step 2 — Detect duration

```text
2 hours 35 minutes
```

### Step 3 — Normalize

```text
11:40 PM → 23:40
```

### Step 4 — Convert to seconds

```text
23 × 3600 + 40 × 60
= 85200 seconds
```

Duration:

```text
2 × 3600 + 35 × 60
= 9300 seconds
```

### Step 5 — Add

```text
85200 + 9300 = 94500
```

### Step 6 — Handle day boundary

One day is:

```text
86400 seconds
```

Therefore:

```text
94500 - 86400 = 8100
```

### Step 7 — Convert back

```text
8100 seconds = 2 hours 15 minutes
```

Therefore:

```text
02:15
day_offset = +1
```

Final:

```text
2:15 AM the next day
```
